# Python
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# Frontend
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
# src/codeslides/static/ is intentionally tracked: it's the built
# frontend bundle the server serves, and committing it means `codeslides
# edit`/`present` works right after a fresh checkout without a manual
# `npm install && npm run build` step in frontend/.

# TODO.md #64: a generated copy of the subset of src/codeslides/ proven
# to run inside Pyodide unmodified (scripts/sync-pyscript-modules.mjs),
# regenerated by predev/prebuild -- never hand-edited, so not tracked
# here (same "generated input, not source" reasoning as node_modules/
# above). The BUILT copy under src/codeslides/static/ is still tracked
# normally, same as every other build output already is.
frontend/public/codeslides_pyscript/

# Editors / OS
.idea/
.DS_Store

# TODO.md #46g-v: per-deck collaborative-edit attribution sidecar
# (serialization.py's attribution_sidecar_path) -- incidental
# collaboration metadata generated by the running server, not lesson
# content meant for version control (same category as a lockfile).
# Applies to this repo's own example decks under examples/; an
# instructor's own lesson repo should likely ignore the same pattern.
*.codeslides-attribution.json
